{"name":"Gotham City","hex":"#757c7d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"city","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large settlement, bigger than a town; sometimes with a specific legal definition, depending on the place.","A settlement granted special status by royal charter or letters patent; traditionally, a settlement with a cathedral regardless of size."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/city"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gotham City","blocks":[{"text":"Gotham City, or simply Gotham, is a fictional city in the Northeastern United States that serves as the primary urban setting in American comic books published by DC Comics. It is best known as the home of the superhero Batman and his allies and foes. Created by writer Bill Finger and artist Bob Kane, Gotham was first identified as Batman's place of residence in Batman #4 and has since been the primary setting for stories featuring the character. While affluent, civic-minded families like the Waynes strive to rebuild Gotham City, it remains traditionally depicted as a crime-ridden dystopia, utterly consumed by institutional corruption, predatory mob syndicates, and erratic lunatics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/93/Gotham_City_-_Batman_107_%28April_2021%29.png/330px-Gotham_City_-_Batman_107_%28April_2021%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gotham_City","wikidata":"Q732858"},{"title":"Gotham City (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Gotham City\" is a song by American R&B singer and songwriter R. Kelly, based on the fictional city of the same name. It was featured on the soundtrack to the film Batman & Robin, and was released as a single on June 3, 1997 by Warner Bros. and Jive Records. The song reached number nine on both the US Billboard Hot 100 and Hot R&B Singles charts. In Europe, it peaked within the top 10 in Germany, Hungary, the Netherlands, Sweden, Switzerland and the UK, and within the top 20 in Iceland, Ireland and Scotland. The music video for the song was directed by Hype Williams and filmed in New York City. A remix version for the song was released featuring rapper Strings with a video also directed by Williams."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/87/Gotham_City_R._Kelly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gotham_City_(song)","wikidata":"Q654286"},{"title":"Gotham (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Gotham is an American superhero crime drama television series developed by Bruno Heller, produced by Warner Bros. Television and based on characters from the Batman mythos in comic books published by DC Comics. It features an ensemble cast that includes Ben McKenzie as James \"Jim\" Gordon, Donal Logue as Harvey Bullock, and David Mazouz as Bruce Wayne. The show follows Gordon's early days at the Gotham City Police Department following the murder of Bruce's parents, as well as the origin stories of Batman's infamous rogues gallery. The series premiered on Fox on September 22, 2014, and ended on April 25, 2019, after five seasons totalling 100 episodes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gotham_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q15726959"},{"title":"City","blocks":[{"text":"A city is a human settlement of a substantial size. The term \"city\" has different meanings around the world and in some places the settlement can be very small. Even where the term is limited to larger settlements, there is no universally agreed definition of the lower numerical boundary for their size. In a more specific sense, a city can be defined as a permanent and densely populated place with administratively defined boundaries whose members work primarily on non-agricultural tasks. Cities generally have extensive systems for housing, transportation, sanitation, utilities, land use, production of goods, and communication. Their density facilitates interaction between people, government organizations, and businesses, sometimes benefiting different parties in the process, such as improving the efficiency of goods and service distribution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg/330px-Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City","wikidata":"Q515"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/85/Gotham-City-1881.jpg/330px-Gotham-City-1881.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/85/Gotham-City-1881.jpg/330px-Gotham-City-1881.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gotham City in 1881 from Batman: Gates of Gotham (April 2011). Art by Trevor McCarthy.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGotham-City-1881.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/89/Gotham_City_Batman_Vol_1_615.png/330px-Gotham_City_Batman_Vol_1_615.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/89/Gotham_City_Batman_Vol_1_615.png/330px-Gotham_City_Batman_Vol_1_615.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Airships are commonly depicted flying over Gotham City.[36] Art by Jim Lee.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGotham_City_Batman_Vol_1_615.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Helsinki_Railway_station_tower_%26_statues.jpg/500px-Helsinki_Railway_station_tower_%26_statues.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Helsinki_Railway_station_tower_%26_statues.jpg/500px-Helsinki_Railway_station_tower_%26_statues.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Art Deco and Art Nouveau buildings, such as Helsinki Central Railway Station, inspired the look of Gotham in the 1989 film Batman.[38]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHelsinki_Railway_station_tower_%26_statues.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/fa/Batman_Knight_over_Gotham.jpg/330px-Batman_Knight_over_Gotham.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/fa/Batman_Knight_over_Gotham.jpg/330px-Batman_Knight_over_Gotham.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Batman overlooks Gotham, his home city. Art by Alex Ross.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABatman_Knight_over_Gotham.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/23/Gotham_skyline.JPG/330px-Gotham_skyline.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/23/Gotham_skyline.JPG/330px-Gotham_skyline.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gotham City's skyline in the 1989 Batman film","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGotham_skyline.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b3/Gotham_Knight_Skyline.jpg/250px-Gotham_Knight_Skyline.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b3/Gotham_Knight_Skyline.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b3/Gotham_Knight_Skyline.jpg/250px-Gotham_Knight_Skyline.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Gotham City skyline in Batman: Gotham Knight (2008)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGotham_Knight_Skyline